{'symbol': 'TSN', 'date': '2019-11-12 11:30:00', 'title': 'TYSON FOODS REPORTS Q4 ADJ EARNINGS PER SHARE OF $1.21', 'text': "TYSON FOODS REPORTS FOURTH QUARTER AND FISCAL 2019 RESULTS.Q4 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.21.Q4 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.01.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.29 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES HIGH SINGLE DIGIT ADJUSTED EPS GROWTH OVER TIME.TYSON FOODS - CURRENTLY EXPECT TO MEET OR EXCEED LONG-TERM EARNINGS ALGORITHM OF HIGH SINGLE-DIGIT ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE GROWTH FOR FISCAL 2020.QTRLY BEEF SALES $3,861 MILLION VERSUS $3,913 MILLION.FOR FISCAL 2020, BELIEVE BEEF SEGMENT'S ADJUSTED OPERATING MARGIN WILL BE 6.5% TO 7.5%, ABSENT IMPACTS FROM ASF..QTRLY PORK SALES $1,258 MILLION VERSUS $1,134 MILLION.FOR FISCAL 2020, BELIEVE PORK SEGMENT'S ADJUSTED OPERATING MARGIN WILL BE 6% TO 8%, ABSENT IMPACTS FROM ASF..QTRLY CHICKEN SALES $3,447 MILLION VERSUS $3,115 MILLION.FOR FISCAL 2020, BELIEVE CHICKEN SEGMENT'S ADJUSTED OPERATING MARGIN WILL BE 6% TO 8%, ABSENT IMPACTS FROM ASF.TYSON FOODS - BEEF SALES VOLUME FELL IN QUARTER DUE TO REDUCTION IN PROCESSING CAPACITY FROM TEMPORARY CLOSURE OF FACILITY AS RESULT OF A FIRE.TYSON FOODS - EXPECT IMPROVED RESULTS IN FISCAL 2020 FROM IMPROVEMENT IN LEGACY FOREIGN OPERATIONS.EXPECT INDUSTRY FED CATTLE SUPPLIES TO INCREASE APPROXIMATELY 2% IN FISCAL 2020.EXPECT RAW MATERIAL COSTS TO RISE IN FISCAL 2020 AS COMPARED TO FISCAL 2019.EXPECT INDUSTRY HOG SUPPLIES TO INCREASE APPROXIMATELY 3% IN FISCAL 2020.EXPECT TO RECOVER INCREASED RAW MATERIAL COSTS IN FISCAL 2020 THROUGH PRICING."}{'symbol': 'TSN', 'date': '2019-11-11 22:30:00', 'title': 'TYSON FOODS, INC. INCREASES PREVIOUSLY DECLARED QUARTERLY DIVIDEND ON CLASS A COMMON STOCK AND CLASS B COMMON STOCK, PAYABLE ON DECEMBER 13, 2019 AND DECLARES QUARTERLY DIVIDEND ON CLASS A COMMON STOCK AND CLASS B COMMON STOCK PAYABLE ON MARCH 13, 2020', 'text': 'EFFECTIVE NOVEMBER 11, 2019, THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS OF TYSON FOODS, INC. INCREASED THE QUARTERLY DIVIDEND PREVIOUSLY DECLARED ON AUGUST 8, 2019, TO $0.42 PER SHARE ON CLASS A COMMON STOCK AND $0.378 PER SHARE ON CLASS B COMMON STOCK. THE INCREASED QUARTERLY DIVIDEND IS PAYABLE ON DECEMBER 13, 2019, TO SHAREHOLDERS OF RECORD AT THE CLOSE OF BUSINESS ON NOVEMBER 29, 2019. THE BOARD ALSO DECLARED A QUARTERLY DIVIDEND OF $0.42 PER SHARE ON CLASS A COMMON STOCK AND $0.378 PER SHARE ON CLASS B COMMON STOCK, PAYABLE ON MARCH 13, 2020, TO SHAREHOLDERS OF RECORD AT THE CLOSE OF BUSINESS ON FEBRUARY 28, 2020. COMPANY ANTICIPATE THE REMAINING QUARTERLY DIVIDENDS IN FISCAL 2020 WILL BE $0.42 AND $0.378 PER SHARE OF CLASS A AND CLASS B STOCK, RESPECTIVELY. THIS RESULTS IN AN ANNUAL DIVIDEND RATE IN FISCAL 2020 OF $1.68 FOR CLASS A SHARES AND $1.512 FOR CLASS B SHARES, OR A 12% INCREASE COMPARED TO THE FISCAL 2019 ANNUAL DIVIDEND RATE.'}{'symbol': 'TSN', 'date': '2019-11-12 11:30:00', 'title': 'TYSON FOODS REPORTS Q4 ADJ EARNINGS PER SHARE OF $1.21', 'text': "TYSON FOODS REPORTS FOURTH QUARTER AND FISCAL 2019 RESULTS.Q4 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.21.Q4 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.01.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.29 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES HIGH SINGLE DIGIT ADJUSTED EPS GROWTH OVER TIME.TYSON FOODS - CURRENTLY EXPECT TO MEET OR EXCEED LONG-TERM EARNINGS ALGORITHM OF HIGH SINGLE-DIGIT ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE GROWTH FOR FISCAL 2020.QTRLY BEEF SALES $3,861 MILLION VERSUS $3,913 MILLION.FOR FISCAL 2020, BELIEVE BEEF SEGMENT'S ADJUSTED OPERATING MARGIN WILL BE 6.5% TO 7.5%, ABSENT IMPACTS FROM ASF..QTRLY PORK SALES $1,258 MILLION VERSUS $1,134 MILLION.FOR FISCAL 2020, BELIEVE PORK SEGMENT'S ADJUSTED OPERATING MARGIN WILL BE 6% TO 8%, ABSENT IMPACTS FROM ASF..QTRLY CHICKEN SALES $3,447 MILLION VERSUS $3,115 MILLION.FOR FISCAL 2020, BELIEVE CHICKEN SEGMENT'S ADJUSTED OPERATING MARGIN WILL BE 6% TO 8%, ABSENT IMPACTS FROM ASF.TYSON FOODS - BEEF SALES VOLUME FELL IN QUARTER DUE TO REDUCTION IN PROCESSING CAPACITY FROM TEMPORARY CLOSURE OF FACILITY AS RESULT OF A FIRE.TYSON FOODS - EX